n Jackson, who is sixth in the FBS with 3,005 passing yards, will miss at least the next two games with an upper-body injury.","published":"2026-11-17T20:53:17.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50513204/north-texas-qb-tayven-jackson-upper-body-injury","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Defiant Dabo Swinney says Clemson's 'gonna win a bunch more'","description":"Despite going through a self-described \"rough patch\" over the past two seasons, Clemson coach Dabo Swinney is resolute in his belief that he and the Tigers have a lot more wins ahead of them.","published":"2026-11-17T20:37:09.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50512833/defiant-dabo-swinney-says-clemson-gonna-win-bunch-more","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Andrea Adelson","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5127738/ashton-hampton","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ashton_Hampton"},"pick":{"pick":10,"round":1,"team":"TB","provisional":false},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Ashton Hampton","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ashton_Hampton","description":"American football player (born 2006)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:37:48Z","intro":"Ashton Hampton (born January 9, 2006) is an American college football cornerback for the Clemson Tigers.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Hampton attended Florida State University High School in Tallahassee, Florida, where he played cornerback and wide receiver. He was the All-Big Bend Defensive Player of the Year his senior year after recording 64 tackles and three interceptions. During his career he had 92 tackles and six interceptions on defense and 115 receptions for 1,797 yards and 21 touchdowns as a receiver. Hampton committed to Clemson University to play college football."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Hampton earned immediate playing time his freshman year at Clemson in 2024. He started four of 14 games and had 30 tackles and two interception, one that was returned for a touchdown. He started all 13 games his sophomore year in 2025, recording 45 tackles and one interception."}]}}